<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fritzlar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fritzlar is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the Eder river. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-boniface">Saint Boniface</a> founded a church and monastery there after felling the sacred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thor">Donar</a>'s Oak nearby in 723, and it became a centre of the Christian mission in Hesse. In 919 Frankish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> nobles elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a> at Fritzlar, the first Saxon to take the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fritzlar.jpg" alt="Fritzlar" width="320" height="137" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Axel Hindemith · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fritzlar_vom_B%C3%BCraberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
